her that ran from the 215.40\u2013215.60 area in early July all the way to the 219.62 peak \u2014 a move of roughly 420 pips across nine sessions. Since that high, price has retraced in a tight, overlapping sequence of lower closes, with daily ranges compressing noticeably. The 218.00\u2013218.50 band has acted as a congestion zone for much of the past fortnight, and the pair has now slipped beneath it, closing yesterday at 217.60. This is the first meaningful break of that consolidation floor, and it shifts the near-term tone cautiously toward the downside. The prior reaction zone around 215.57, which attracted three separate responses during the initial July rally, now represents the first meaningful structural reference below current price. Deeper still, the 214.65 area \u2014 a four-touch support zone \u2014 would be the level that, if tested, would suggest the entire mid-July advance is being unwound more substantially.\n\nOn the H1 chart, the picture is one of quiet, methodical drift. Price slid from the 218.40s during the late Monday afternoon session yesterday, found a low around 217.49 in the early hours of Tuesday, and has since stabilised in a narrow 217.57\u2013217.83 range through the London morning. There is no sign of aggressive buying interest reclaiming the 218.00 level, and each attempt to push higher has stalled well short of that figure. The intraday structure looks like a market that is consolidating after a leg lower rather than staging a recovery \u2014 sellers appear to retain the marginal advantage on the shorter timeframe.\n\nToday's economic calendar is empty of scheduled high-impact events, which means price action is likely to be driven by broader risk sentiment and any cross-market flows rather than data surprises. Thin catalysts can cut both ways \u2014 quieter sessions sometimes allow technical levels to hold cleanly, but they can also see exaggerated moves if positioning shifts.\n\nThe desk's neutral bias reflects the tension between the broader uptrend from late June and the current corrective pressure. What would change the read toward a more constructive picture is a decisive reclaim of the 218.50 area on a closing basis, suggesting the retracement has run its course. Conversely, a sustained break and close beneath 217.00 would open the path toward the 215.57 prior reaction zone and would materially weaken the bullish structural case built over the past month.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}